{
  "decision": "Neither replaces the prototype. Threshold calibration suppresses reviewed bass-core triggers but loses too many kicks. Adding six band-local spectral measurements improves the calibrated 70ms result, from 86 matches/44 unmatched to 98/41; original prototype is118/52. At50ms the bandwise result is66/73 versus calibrated base65/65 and prototype116/54. Continue treating fusion as exploratory.",
  "protocol": "Nested song exclusion: outer test song excluded from all fits, normalisation and threshold choice. Each inner prediction uses the other seven songs. Fixed threshold grid .50 through .975 step .025 plus .99,.999,1.01. Select maximum inner70ms matches subject to aggregate wide-association-extra and kick-free-core-extra budgets no worse than inner prototype. Ties prefer fewer wide extras then higher cutoff. Refit on eight and apply selected threshold to outer song. Same candidate grid, 40ms horizon rounded up to hop boundary, 60ms refractory, frozen labels and all other fitting choices.",
  "bandwise": "Exactly six added features: maximum relative positive flux and first15-minus-last15ms log-frequency centroid per30-140,140-1000,1000-8000Hz band, from the same trailing2048 Hann FFT. Original nine features preserved bitwise; no additional evidence wait. Offline extraction recomputes the FFT; this is not a runtime-optimised implementation.",
  "validation": "Twelve new focused tests pass: five bandwise, seven calibration. Includes prefix causality, frozen-column/grid equality, band isolation, outer-song perturbation invariance, seven-song inner fits, threshold ties, output timing/refractory and original-five score-schema regression. Exact fixed0.5 output replay matches all nine prior songs. Lead independently checked every source/label/baseline hash, fold exclusion, chosen threshold, refractory interval and aggregate score. Initial base run failed in reporting because original-five strict scores omit pairs; repaired using missed-label set differences, regression tested, then repeated unchanged experiment.",
  "limitations": "Nine previously explored songs and provisional labels; no untouched external validation. Wide association is diagnostic, not proof of source identity. Inner budgets do not guarantee outer or per-song budgets. The actual false-trigger counts differ; this is not an exactly matched-error comparison. At70ms the bandwise result improves versus calibrated nine-feature fusion; at50ms extra counts worsen. All four reviewed bass-only cores are clean, but positive passages retain many extra triggers. No native runtime, live audio or GPU changes.",
